From 8cef507f3cd818462f8873585af3fb91c8039e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:46:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth and Local players: now-playing view, library
 browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

NowPlaying, shared by both: album art (or a music-note placeholder) with
rounded corners and sized to fit, title / artist / album (long names end
in "…"; messages such as "Nothing playing" wrap), a progress bar with
elapsed and total time, and previous / round play-pause / next.

- Bluetooth: the phone's track (BlueZ AVRCP), position counted on between
  BlueZ's reports, the device's name; Android Auto's media with its album
  art when that is playing. Without a player it says so and points to
  Settings > Phone. AVRCP can't seek, so the bar only shows progress.
- Local: a folder browser (folder and song icons, up, folder name, make it
  the music home) beside the now-playing view. Songs show title and artist
  from their tags and cover art embedded in the file (TagLib 2 pictures);
  MP3, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis/Opus and WAV. Browsing doesn't stop the
  music: the folder on screen becomes the playlist when a song in it is
  tapped.
